#
# ---- N8000 tuning patch -----------------------------------------------------
# Evidence for every line is in dist/n8000-tweaks/FINDINGS.md.
# Nothing was REMOVED from this file. The audit found 36 properties that no
# binary in /system reads, but that scan cannot see apps in /data - and
# properties like ro.build.characteristics are read by third-party apps - so
# deleting them would risk app-visible behaviour for no measurable gain.
# Only four existing values were changed; the rest is additive.
#
# USB. default.prop ships persist.sys.usb.config=none, and init.usb.rc does
#   on boot && property:persist.sys.usb.config=*
#       setprop sys.usb.config ${persist.sys.usb.config}
# with the "none" handler calling `stop adbd`. So the device comes up with no
# USB function at all - no MTP, no ADB - until the framework's UsbDeviceManager
# boots and sets one. That self-corrects on a healthy boot, but if the ROM ever
# hangs or bootloops before the framework starts, USB is dead exactly when you
# need adb to find out why.
#
# mtp,adb is handled by init.smdk4x12.usb.rc (idProduct 6860). persist.*
# properties are re-read from /data once it mounts, so whatever you pick in
# Settings still wins - this value only applies on a fresh flash, which is
# precisely the case worth insuring. ro.adb.secure=1 is untouched, so a new
# host still has to be authorised by RSA key.
persist.sys.usb.config=mtp,adb
#
# I/O scheduler. The kernel default is cfq, built for rotating disks and pure
# overhead on eMMC. /system/etc/init/lineage-iosched.rc already ships the
# switching machinery and simply never sets this property. Going through it
# makes init apply the scheduler to every block device, SD card included.
persist.sys.io.scheduler=row
#
# dex2oat parallelism. default.prop (in the ramdisk) pins this to a single
# thread on a quad-core SoC. build.prop is loaded after default.prop, so
# redefining it here wins without touching the ramdisk.
dalvik.vm.dex2oat-threads=2
dalvik.vm.image-dex2oat-threads=2
dalvik.vm.dex2oat-swap=true
#
# The one genuinely useful effect of ro.config.low_ram=true, without that
# flag's cost: low_ram would disable NotificationListenerService and voice
# interaction outright. Read directly by ActiveServices.
ro.config.max_starting_bg=1
#
# speed-profile keeps hot code compiled while using far less /data than speed.
pm.dexopt.install=speed-profile
pm.dexopt.bg-dexopt=speed-profile
pm.dexopt.boot=verify
pm.dexopt.inactive=verify
# ---- end N8000 tuning patch ------------------------------------------------
